mpairment` values. Each selected helper snapshots the three pointed\nto floats and then writes `R`, `G`, and `B` in order, making the five pointer\nalias partitions observable input shapes. There are no runtime flags, lengths,\nformats, element types, byte-order options, conditional-compilation branches,\nor lower-level public entry points.\n\nEvery row is exercised with reproducible randomized `f32` bit patterns,\nincluding ordinary finite values, signed zeros, subnormals, infinities, and\nNaNs.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `colourblind` | `cbProtanopia`; `R`, `G`, and `B` are distinct pointers | [ ] |\n| 2 | `colourblind` | `cbProtanopia`; `R == G`, with distinct `B` | [ ] |\n| 3 | `colourblind` | `cbProtanopia`; `R == B`, with distinct `G` | [ ] |\n| 4 | `colourblind` | `cbProtanopia`; `G == B`, with distinct `R` | [ ] |\n| 5 | `colourblind` | `cbProtanopia`; `R == G == B` | [ ] |\n| 6 | `colourblind` | `cbDeuteranopia`; `R`, `G`, and `B` are distinct pointers | [ ] |\n| 7 | `colourblind` | `cbDeuteranopia`; `R == G`, with distinct `B` | [ ] |\n| 8 | `colourblind` | `cbDeuteranopia`; `R == B`, with distinct `G` | [ ] |\n| 9 | `colourblind` | `cbDeuteranopia`; `G == B`, with distinct `R` | [ ] |\n| 10 | `colourblind` | `cbDeuteranopia`; `R == G == B` | [ ] |\n| 11 | `colourblind` | `cbTritanopia`; `R`, `G`, and `B` are distinct pointers | [ ] |\n| 12 | `colourblind` | `cbTritanopia`; `R == G`, with distinct `B` | [ ] |\n| 13 | `colourblind` | `cbTritanopia`; `R == B`, with distinct `G` | [ ] |\n| 14 | `colourblind` | `cbTritanopia`; `G == B`, with distinct `R` | [ ] |\n| 15 | `colourblind` | `cbTritanopia`; `R == G == B` | [ ] |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
